::ALG2_U03_L01_Q05::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U03_L01_Q05<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.AE.7; MLA.A2.AE.8<br><br>Question:<br>Rewrite a<sup>5/2</sup> in radical form. {
= &radic;(a<sup>5</sup>)#Correct. The denominator 2 gives the square root, and the numerator 5 gives the power.
~ &radic;<sup>5</sup>(a<sup>2</sup>)#This reverses or misuses the parts of the rational exponent. In a<sup>m/n</sup>, n is the root index and m is the power on the radicand.
